# CannyValley — System Architecture

> **CannyValley** is an AI-vs-Real image classification system built with PyTorch. It trains a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to distinguish between AI-generated and real images using the CIFAKE dataset.

---

## High-Level Pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph DataSources["🌐 Data Sources"]
        KG["Kaggle Hub\n(birdy654/cifake)"]
        HF1["HuggingFace\n(Hemg/AI-vs-Real-images)"]
        HF2["HuggingFace\n(bitmind/AI-vs-Real-Dataset)"]
    end

    subgraph Ingestion["📥 Data Ingestion"]
        DL["Dataset Downloader\n(kagglehub / datasets lib)"]
    end

    subgraph Preprocessing["🔧 Preprocessing"]
        TX["Transforms Pipeline"]
        IF["ImageFolder Loader"]
        DLR["DataLoader\n(batch=32)"]
    end

    subgraph Model["🧠 CNN Model"]
        CONV["Conv Layers\n(3 blocks)"]
        FC["Fully Connected\n(Dense Layers)"]
    end

    subgraph Training["🏋️ Training Loop"]
        OPT["Adam Optimizer\n(lr=0.001, wd=0.01)"]
        LOSS["CrossEntropy Loss"]
        EP["Epoch Iterator\n(50 epochs)"]
    end

    subgraph Evaluation["📊 Evaluation"]
        ACC["Accuracy Calculator"]
        VIZ["Visualization\n(matplotlib)"]
    end

    KG --> DL
    HF1 -.->|alternative| DL
    HF2 -.->|alternative| DL
    DL --> TX
    TX --> IF
    IF --> DLR
    DLR --> EP
    EP --> CONV
    CONV --> FC
    FC --> LOSS
    LOSS --> OPT
    OPT -->|update weights| CONV
    DLR -->|test set| ACC
    ACC --> VIZ
    EP -->|loss curve| VIZ
```

---

## CNN Architecture Detail

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    INPUT["Input Image\n3 × 224 × 224"] --> C1

    subgraph Block1["Conv Block 1"]
        C1["Conv2d\n3 → 32, 3×3, pad=1"]
        R1["ReLU"]
        P1["MaxPool2d\n2×2"]
        C1 --> R1 --> P1
    end

    P1 --> C2

    subgraph Block2["Conv Block 2"]
        C2["Conv2d\n32 → 64, 3×3, pad=1"]
        R2["ReLU"]
        P2["MaxPool2d\n2×2"]
        C2 --> R2 --> P2
    end

    P2 --> C3

    subgraph Block3["Conv Block 3"]
        C3["Conv2d\n64 → 64, 3×3, pad=1"]
        R3["ReLU"]
        P3["MaxPool2d\n2×2"]
        C3 --> R3 --> P3
    end

    P3 --> FL["Flatten\n64 × 28 × 28 = 50,176"]
    FL --> FC1["Linear\n50,176 → 512"]
    FC1 --> R4["ReLU"]
    R4 --> FC2["Linear\n512 → 2"]
    FC2 --> OUT["Output\n(REAL / FAKE)"]
```

---

## Data Preprocessing Pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    RAW["Raw Image\n(variable size)"] --> RS["Resize\nto 256px"]
    RS --> CC["CenterCrop\n224 × 224"]
    CC --> TT["ToTensor\n(0–1 float)"]
    TT --> NM["Normalize\nμ=[.485,.456,.406]\nσ=[.229,.224,.225]"]
    NM --> READY["Preprocessed Tensor\n3 × 224 × 224"]
```

---

## Training & Evaluation Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph TrainPhase["Training Phase"]
        direction TB
        TE["For each epoch (1..50)"]
        TB["For each batch in train_loader"]
        FW["Forward Pass → outputs"]
        CL["Compute CrossEntropyLoss"]
        BP["Backward Pass (loss.backward)"]
        US["Optimizer Step (Adam)"]
        TL["Accumulate train_loss"]
        TE --> TB --> FW --> CL --> BP --> US --> TL
        TL -->|next batch| TB
        TL -->|epoch done| TE
    end

    subgraph EvalPhase["Evaluation Phase"]
        direction TB
        EM["model.eval() + no_grad"]
        EB["For each batch in test_loader"]
        EF["Forward Pass → outputs"]
        EP["argmax → predictions"]
        EA["Accumulate correct predictions"]
        EM --> EB --> EF --> EP --> EA
        EA -->|next batch| EB
    end

    subgraph Output["Output & Visualization"]
        LC["Training Loss Curve\n(matplotlib)"]
        AS["Test Accuracy Score"]
        SG["Sample Grid\n(actual vs predicted)"]
    end

    TrainPhase --> EvalPhase
    TrainPhase --> LC
    EvalPhase --> AS
    EvalPhase --> SG
```

---

## Component Summary

| Component | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **Data Sourcing** | `kagglehub`, `datasets` (HuggingFace) | Download CIFAKE or alternative datasets |
| **Preprocessing** | `torchvision.transforms` | Resize, crop, normalize images to 224×224 tensors |
| **Data Loading** | `torchvision.datasets.ImageFolder`, `torch.utils.data.DataLoader` | Batch images with labels (REAL=0, FAKE=1) |
| **Model** | `torch.nn.Module` (custom CNN) | 3 conv blocks → flatten → 2 FC layers → binary output |
| **Loss Function** | `torch.nn.CrossEntropyLoss` | Multi-class cross-entropy for binary classification |
| **Optimizer** | `torch.optim.Adam` | Adaptive learning rate (lr=0.001, weight_decay=0.01) |
| **Evaluation** | PyTorch inference loop | Calculate test accuracy via argmax comparison |
| **Visualization** | `matplotlib` | Plot loss curve and sample prediction grid |
| **Environment** | Google Colab / Jupyter (Anaconda) | Interactive notebook execution with optional GPU |

---

## Key Hyperparameters

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Batch Size | 32 |
| Epochs | 50 |
| Learning Rate | 0.001 |
| Weight Decay | 0.01 |
| Image Size | 224 × 224 |
| Normalization | ImageNet mean/std |
| Output Classes | 2 (REAL, FAKE) |
